# Security Guidelines Cursor Rules

## Input Validation

- Validate all user inputs at the API level
- Use Pydantic models for request validation
- Implement proper type checking for all parameters
- Sanitize file uploads and check file types
- Validate file sizes and content
- Use allowlist approach for acceptable inputs

## Authentication & Authorization

- Implement proper JWT token validation
- Use secure token storage (httpOnly cookies)
- Implement proper session management
- Use role-based access control (RBAC)
- Secure sensitive endpoints with proper decorators
- Implement proper logout functionality

## Data Protection

- Use environment variables for sensitive configuration
- Never hardcode secrets, API keys, or passwords
- Encrypt sensitive data at rest
- Use HTTPS in production environments
- Implement proper CORS policies
- Use secure headers (HSTS, CSP, etc.)

## API Security

- Implement rate limiting to prevent abuse
- Use proper HTTP status codes for errors
- Don't expose internal error details to clients
- Implement request size limits
- Use parameterized queries to prevent injection
- Validate all API parameters

## Error Handling

- Don't expose sensitive information in error messages
- Log security events appropriately
- Use generic error messages for client-facing errors
- Implement proper audit logging
- Handle exceptions securely

## File Security

- Validate file uploads thoroughly
- Check file types and content
- Implement file size limits
- Store files in secure locations
- Use secure file naming conventions
- Implement proper file access controls

## Database Security

- Use parameterized queries only
- Implement proper database user permissions
- Use connection pooling securely
- Encrypt sensitive database fields
- Implement proper backup security
- Use database migrations safely

## Logging & Monitoring

- Log security events and errors
- Don't log sensitive information
- Implement proper log rotation
- Monitor for suspicious activities
- Use structured logging for security events

## Dependencies

- Keep dependencies updated
- Use dependency scanning tools
- Avoid using deprecated packages
- Check for known vulnerabilities
- Use trusted package sources only

## Environment Security

- Use different configurations for different environments
- Secure production environment properly
- Implement proper access controls
- Use secure deployment practices
- Monitor production environment 